# get - get data from the server
# post - create resource in the server
put - full update
patch - partial update of resource
delete - delete data from the server


pytest = control order execution
pytest dependency feature - make dependency b/w tests
if main test fails, then dependency tests will be skipped


3 imp rules for API testing
1.Pre-conditions - content type, set cookies, add auth, add param, set headers
2.Actions - get, put, post, delete
3.Validations - Status code, Response body, Response time, content-type, headers and cookies

Request --> Payload --> Request Body --> JSON format
Post method will generate ID using this we can Update and delete the resource

ways to create request payload
1 - Dictionary
2 - JSON module
3 - Python custom class
4 - DataClasses
5 - External json file

pytest fixtures - functions(with setup and teardown steps)

setup()
yield
teardown()

fixture function needs to be passed as an argument to test functions
fixture function will be defined in conftest.py

